{number: 125}
{title: O Come, O Come, Emmanuel}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C] come, O come, Em-[F] manu-[C] el,
And ransom captive [F] Isra-[C] el,
That [Am] mourns in lonely [Dm] exile [G] here
Un-[C] til the Son of [F] God ap-[C] pear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Re-[G] joice! Re-[Am] joice! Em-[F] manu-[C] el
Shall [Dm] come to thee, O [G7] Isra-[C] el!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O [C] come, Thou Rod of [F] Jesse, [C] free
Thine own from Satan's [F] tyran-[C] ny;
From [Am] depths of hell Thy [Dm] people [G] save
And [C] give them vict'ry [F] o'er the [C] grave.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [C] come, Thou Dayspring, [F] come and [C] cheer
Our spirits by Thine [F] advent [C] here;
And [Am] drive away the [Dm] shades of [G] night,
And [C] pierce the clouds and [F] bring us [C] light!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [C] come, Thou Key of [F] David, [C] come
And open wide our [F] heavenly [C] home;
Make [Am] safe the way that [Dm] leads on [G] high,
And [C] close the path to [F] mise-[C] ry.
{end_of_verse}
